### ============================================
### Cross-Tenant User Tests
### Test users working across multiple tenants
### ============================================

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api
@acme_subdomain = acme
@techstart_subdomain = techstart

### ============================================
### Scenario 1: John logs into Acme Corporation
### ============================================

### 1. Login as John to Acme (Tenant 1)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "email": "john.sales@tawasol.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# Save the access token from response
# @name loginAcme
### Expected: 200 OK with tokens, John's role is SALES

### 2. Get John's profile in Acme
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

### Expected: John Sales, role: SALES, tenantId: Acme

### 3. List all tenants John has access to
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/my-tenants HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Expected: Array with 2 tenants (Acme and TechStart)

### ============================================
### Scenario 2: John switches to TechStart
### ============================================

### 4. Switch to TechStart tenant
# First, get the tenantId from the my-tenants response
# Then use it here (replace with actual ID)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/switch-tenant HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "PASTE_TECHSTART_TENANT_ID_HERE"
}

# @name switchTenant
### Expected: 200 OK with new tokens for TechStart tenant

### 5. Get John's profile in TechStart (using new token)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{switchTenant.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

### Expected: John Sales, role: SALES, tenantId: TechStart

### ============================================
### Scenario 3: John logs directly into TechStart
### ============================================

### 6. Login as John to TechStart (Tenant 2)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

{
  "email": "john.sales@techstart.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# @name loginTechStart
### Expected: 200 OK with tokens, John's role is SALES

### 7. Get John's profile in TechStart
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTechStart.response.body.data.accessToken}}
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

### Expected: John Sales, role: SALES, tenantId: TechStart

### 8. List all tenants (should show both again)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/my-tenants HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginTechStart.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Expected: Array with 2 tenants (Acme and TechStart)

### ============================================
### Scenario 4: Admin works across both tenants
### ============================================

### 9. Login as Admin to Acme
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "email": "admin@tawasol.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# @name adminAcme
### Expected: 200 OK, role: ADMIN

### 10. List admin's tenants
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/my-tenants HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{adminAcme.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Expected: Array with 2 tenants (Acme and TechStart), both with ADMIN role

### 11. Login as Admin to TechStart
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{techstart_subdomain}}

{
  "email": "admin@techstart.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# @name adminTechStart
### Expected: 200 OK, role: ADMIN

### ============================================
### Scenario 5: Tenant isolation test
### ============================================

### 12. Mike Support (only in Acme) tries to login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
X-Tenant-Subdomain: {{acme_subdomain}}

{
  "email": "mike.support@tawasol.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

# @name mikeSales
### Expected: 200 OK

### 13. Mike checks his tenants (should only have Acme)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/my-tenants HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{mikeSales.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### Expected: Array with 1 tenant (Acme only)

### 14. Mike tries to switch to TechStart (should fail)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/switch-tenant HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{mikeSales.response.body.data.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "PASTE_TECHSTART_TENANT_ID_HERE"
}

### Expected: 403 Forbidden - You do not have access to this tenant

### ============================================
### Summary:
### - John and Admin can work across both tenants
### - Mike only has access to Acme
### - Users can switch tenants without re-login
### - Same email (via UserProfile) links accounts
### ============================================
